-- two reports on one compound under one condition with different values: no function of the compound and
-- the condition agrees with both. This is the sharpened form of reports-disagree-no-function, and the
-- sharpening is the point. That statement treated every disagreement alike, so it convicted a temperature
-- series along with a contradiction. Here the condition is in the hypothesis: two reports must agree on
-- it before their disagreement means anything. The Classification and Labelling Inventory's disagreeing
-- notifications are of this kind -- one substance, one hazard class, one set of criteria, two answers --
-- and a variable-temperature spectrum is not.
creports-same-cond-disagree : (k : Compound) → (c : Cond) → (r1 : CReport Nat) → (r2 : CReport Nat) → cr-cmp Nat r1 ≡ k → cr-cmp Nat r2 ≡ k → cr-cond Nat r1 ≡ c → cr-cond Nat r2 ≡ c → (cr-value Nat r1 ≡ cr-value Nat r2 → Empty) → ((h : Compound → Cond → Nat) → ((r : CReport Nat) → h (cr-cmp Nat r) (cr-cond Nat r) ≡ cr-value Nat r) → Empty)
creports-same-cond-disagree k c r1 r2 q1 q2 s1 s2 no =
  λ h → λ agrees → no (concat (sym (agrees r1)) (concat (cong-cmp-cond h (cr-cmp Nat r1) k q1 (cr-cond Nat r1) c s1) (concat (cong-cmp-cond h k (cr-cmp Nat r2) (sym q2) c (cr-cond Nat r2) (sym s2)) (agrees r2))))
